<title>USA: Florida late orange harvest in full swing - FASS.</title>
<headline>Florida late orange harvest in full swing - FASS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were a few scattered showers this week in Florida's citrus belt, the Florida Agricultural Statistics Service (FASS), said in it's Weather and Crop News report.</p>
<p>In its weekly update, FASS said new crop fruit is continuing in very good condition and caretakers are irrigating in most well-cared for groves.</p>
<p>Harvest of late oranges is in full swing on the lower east coast, which is usually the last area to be harvested according to FASS. Supplies of current crop Valencia oranges are running low in most areas.</p>
<p>FASS reported an estimated 5,776,000 boxes of Valencia oranges were harvested in the week ended June 1, down from 6,353,000 in the week ended May 26.</p>
<p>((-- New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
